Why: a host off-Space window resolver (ax::bindings::set_off_space_window_resolver) used in place of the built-in remote-token probe, so an embedding app can reach windows on another Space with element ids it remembers and a scan that resumes where it stopped.

copy_ax_windows_including probes element ids 0..2000 from the first id on
every call, within 300 ms. A long-running app's window can sit beyond what
that budget covers (a document window at element id 2531 was measured out of
reach), so every read of it and every action on it is refused. An app hands
out such a window's element only while it is main or focused, and its id
stays the same for the window's life, so a host that watches the app's
window notifications and remembers ids can find it at once. The resolver,
when set, replaces the probe (a miss does not pay both budgets) and keeps its
contract: an AXWindow element for exactly that window id, retained. Without
a resolver nothing changes. Upstreamable as is.

